'' A UDT FIELD INITIALISED FROM A VALUE OF ITS OWN TYPE ('as P q = pp') declined (TKO0994) for
'' every UDT; fbc copies it -- bytes, a string field's deep copy, or the copy constructor -- and
'' builds the field once, not default-constructed first. fbc-modern 1.20's output; see the source.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/field-init-same-type.bas -o tests/codegen/fieldinitsame.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/fieldinitsame.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: R copy
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3 4 5 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: hi
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 9
